#: ../../tools/ebi_proteins_features_tools.rst:63
#: 9e5c08bb64104a2790a08f1a2974caa6
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get molecule processing features for a protein from the "
"EBI Proteins API. Returns signal peptides, transit peptides, mature "
"protein chains, propeptides, and initiator methionine annotations. "
"Essential for understanding how a protein precursor is processed into its"
" functional form. Example: P01308 (Insulin) returns signal peptide "
"(1-24), B chain (25-54), C peptide (57-87), and A chain (90-110) showing "
"the complete insulin processing pathway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ebi_proteins_features_tools.rst:67
#: 4171fb9e342a4dd6a10f7e37283cd1a2
msgid ""
"``accession`` (string) (required) UniProt accession. Examples: 'P01308' "
"(Insulin - classic example), 'P01375' (TNF-alpha), 'P01189' (POMC - "
"multiple peptides), 'P06213' (Insulin receptor)."
msgstr ""

